    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4448654": {
      "title": "Stephens College",
      "description": "Stephens College - Head Basketball Coach In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Head Basketball Coach Stephens College Apply Head Basketball Coach Columbia, MO • Athletics - Basketball Apply Job Type Full-time Description The required essential duties of the Head Basketball Coach are as follows: Coaching at practices, coaching at games, and working individually with student athletes. These duties constitute 95% of the coach’s responsibility. The Head Coach is responsible for supervising assistant coach(es) volunteers and managers. Essential Functions & Responsibilities Performs components of the sports program to include teaching sports specific fundamentals and strategies to student athletes. Responsible for the daily operation of teh basketball program to include budget management. Indentifies and recruits academically qualified student athletes and reinforces student athletes' goal to graduate. Actively supports the endeavors and advancements of Stephens Athletics Department. Operates within the guidelines of Stephens College, AMC, and NAIA Rules and Regulations. Coordinates scheduling and travel arrangements for team travel and recruiting. Promote the academic and athletic well-being of student athletes. Develop and maintain quality relationships within the community both on and off campus. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. An ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of media, administrators, faculty, staff, students, public groups and/or Board of Trustees. Requires the ability to use computers for data entry Requirements Bachelor’s Degree from accredited four-year college or university required. Master’s degree preferred. Demonstrated a minimum of three (3) years of successful coaching experience with NAIA or NCAA preferred. Good interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills Demonstrated ability and success in teaching the skills and fundamentals of the sport Knowledge of and commitment to NAIA rules and regulations. The ability to organize and motivate the student-athletes to maximum performance level in sports and academic achievement. Proven experience in recruiting highly motivated and qualified student-athletes Good organizational and time management skills Demonstrated knowledge of the institution, AMC and NAIA athletics preferred Obtain and/or maintain a Missouri Class E driver’s license and ability to meet university’s insurance requirements for driving college vehicles required Current certification in first aid, cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) and automatic external defibrillator (AED) use is preferred at the time of hire and will be required prior to coaching student-athletes. Position requires extensive internal face to face contact, telephone, email, mailing and other mediums of dialogue with university personnel. Significant interaction faculty, staff and students on a daily basis; work extensively with other departments on campus. ***A professional CV/resume, cover letter, and three references are required to be uploaded when applying for this position.*** Founded in 1833, Stephens College is the second-oldest women's college in the United States, dedicated to providing innovative, experiential, and career-focused education across various disciplines. Located in Columbia, Missouri, Stephens College continues to be a leader in women's education, fostering a community where students are empowered to lead, innovate, and excel. The college also provides flexible, co-educational master’s degrees and certificates for working professionals, and is home to the co-educational Conservatory for the Performing Arts at Stephens College. Ranked (over and over again) as one of the best college towns in America, Columbia, Missouri, is home to 36,000+ college students and 118,000 residents. Columbia — conveniently located approximately 100 miles from both Kansas City and St. Louis — has it all: big-time college sports, film, music and arts festivals, a high-energy arts community, amazing recreation, and a great downtown with lots of places to eat, shop, snack and check out the latest bands. The Columbia community offers outstanding health care options, as well as excellent educational opportunities for every level of student (including our own Children’s School ). Stephens offers an attractive benefits package that includes health insurance, an Employee Assistance Program, Supplemental Retirement Annuity, Faculty/Staff Grants, tuition waivers and tuition paid undergraduate classes for dependents. Full-time staff work 36 hours and are paid for 40 !! Stephens is an Equal Opportunity Employer and will recruit and employ qualified personnel without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, or status as a veteran. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Stephens College: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4438934": {
      "title": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs - Residence Hall Front Desk Assistant - SC Students ONLY",
      "description": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs - Residence Hall Front Desk Assistant - SC Students ONLY In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Stephens College Work Study Jobs > Residence Hall Front Desk Assistant - SC Students ONLY Stephens College Work Study Jobs Apply Residence Hall Front Desk Assistant - SC Students ONLY Student Success & Engagement Apply Job Type Part-time, Temporary Description The Residence Hall Front Desk Assistant serves as the welcoming face of the residence hall community. This position provides exceptional customer service to residents, families, guests, and campus visitors while supporting the daily operations and safety of the residence halls. Front Desk Assistants foster a safe, inclusive, and engaging residential environment by maintaining accurate records, assisting residents with routine needs, monitoring building access, and providing outstanding hospitality. Schedule Approximately 5–20 hours per week; depending on your schedule and departmental needs. Evening, overnight, weekend, and holiday shifts may be available. Flexible scheduling around academic commitments. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Welcome residents, families, guests, faculty, staff, and visitors in a friendly and professional manner. Provide exceptional customer service while creating a warm and inclusive atmosphere. Monitor residence hall access in accordance with College policies. Verify guest check-in procedures and maintain guest logs. Assist with key and access card distribution and documentation. Answer telephones and respond to inquiries. Receive and distribute mail and packages, if applicable. Maintain accurate front desk records and documentation. Monitor common areas and report maintenance, safety, or policy concerns. Support residence hall check-in, check-out, room changes, and break housing operations. Assist with administrative projects and special events. Maintain confidentiality of student information. Perform other duties as assigned. Safety Responsibilities Monitor access to residence halls. Follow guest registration procedures. Report emergencies immediately. Contact professional staff or Campus Safety when appropriate. Maintain accurate documentation of incidents. Understand and follow emergency response procedures. Learning Outcomes Professional customer service Crisis awareness and response Conflict resolution Communication and interpersonal skills Administrative and organizational skills Leadership and responsibility Understanding of residential operations Requirements Minimum Qualifications Currently enrolled as a Stephens College student. Meet institutional requirements for student employment. Maintain a cumulative GPA of 2.5 or higher. Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, professionalism, and sound judgment. Possess excellent customer service and interpersonal skills. Maintain confidentiality. Preferred Qualifications Customer service experience. Residence hall living experience. Experience in a fast-paced environment. Strong organizational skills. Familiarity with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace. Ideal Candidate Friendly and welcoming Dependable and trustworthy Calm under pressure Professional in appearance and communication Detail-oriented Strong problem-solver Comfortable enforcing policies respectfully Team-oriented Committed to creating a safe, caring, and inclusive residential community Salary Description $15.00/hour Apply Stephens College Work Study Jobs Jobs View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Stephens College Work Study Jobs: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4438871": {
      "title": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs - Student Admin Assistant - SC Students ONLY",
