Department-Specific Responsibilities for Residence Life Assist with housing records and occupancy documentation. Prepare materials for resident check-in and check-out. Assist with lockout documentation and key management. Prepare materials for Resident Assistant training and programming. Support communication with residents and families. Department-Specific Responsibilities for Student Engagement Assist with event planning and logistics. Prepare promotional materials and campus communications. Maintain event calendars and registrations. Support student organizations administratively. Assist with campus traditions and engagement initiatives. Support office social media and marketing as appropriate. Learning Outcomes Professional communication Customer service Administrative and organizational skills Time management Problem-solving Teamwork Leadership and professionalism Understanding of higher education administration Requirements Minimum Qualifications Currently enrolled as a Stephens College student. Meet institutional requirements for student employment. Maintain a cumulative GPA of 2.5 or higher. Demonstrate reliability, professionalism, and integrity. Possess strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills. Maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment. Preferred Qualifications Previous customer service experience. Experience working in an office environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office or Google Workspace. Experience using office technology. Strong written communication skills. Previous campus involvement or leadership experience. Ideal Candidate Welcoming and approachable Dependable and punctual Organized and detail-oriented Strong communicator Comfortable interacting with diverse populations Positive ambassador for Stephens College Committed to creating a caring and inclusive campus community Salary Description $15.00/hour Apply Stephens College Work Study Jobs Jobs View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Stephens College Work Study Jobs: Privacy Policy"
