    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4438797": {
      "title": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs",
      "description": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs - Student Engagement Content Creator - SC Students ONLY In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Stephens College Work Study Jobs > Student Engagement Content Creator - SC Students ONLY Stephens College Work Study Jobs Apply Student Engagement Content Creator - SC Students ONLY Student Success & Engagement Apply Job Type Part-time, Temporary Description The Office of Student Success & Engagement is seeking two creative, innovative, and motivated students to serve as Student Engagement Content Creators. These student employees will create engaging digital content that promotes campus life, student involvement, traditions, leadership opportunities, and events while strengthening the Student Success & Engagement brand.  This position is 15-20 hours per week. Working closely with the Director of Student Engagement and in collaboration with the College's Marketing Department, Student Engagement Content Creators will develop authentic content that connects with current students while showcasing the Stephens College experience to prospective students and their families. These positions play an important role in increasing student engagement, supporting recruitment efforts, and creating a vibrant online presence that reflects the student experience at Stephens College. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Create engaging content for the Student Success & Engagement social media platforms, including Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, and emerging platforms. Capture photos and videos during campus events, student programs, and activities. Create Instagram Reels, TikToks, short-form videos, graphics, and promotional materials using Canva, CapCut, Adobe Express, or similar software. Develop original content highlighting student life, traditions, leadership opportunities, campus events, and student involvement. Ensure all content aligns with Stephens College branding and communication standards. Develop creative marketing campaigns that encourage student participation in campus events and activities. Brainstorm innovative ideas that appeal to Gen Z audiences and increase engagement across social media platforms. Stay informed on current social media trends and recommend new strategies to enhance student interaction. Showcase authentic student experiences that support student recruitment and enrollment efforts. Assist in planning and maintaining a social media content calendar. Draft captions and promotional messaging. Schedule and publish approved content. Monitor audience engagement and assist with tracking analytics and campaign performance. Meet regularly with the Director of Student Engagement to plan content and marketing initiatives. Participate in biweekly meetings with the College Marketing Department to align messaging and branding. Collaborate with campus departments and student organizations to promote events and highlight student experiences. Attend major Student Success & Engagement events to capture live content, create pre-event promotions, and produce post-event recaps. Conduct student interviews, testimonials, and behind-the-scenes features. Assist with event setup and breakdown as needed. Learning Outcomes Digital marketing and social media strategy Brand management Content creation and storytelling Photography and videography Graphic design Event marketing and promotion Project management Professional communication Team collaboration Leadership development Social media analytics and audience engagement Requirements Required Qualifications Current Stephens College student in good academic standing. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Creativity and enthusiasm for student engagement and campus life. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Professionalism, dependability, and ability to meet deadlines. Willingness to work occasional evenings and weekends during major campus events. Preferred Qualifications Experience creating content for Instagram, TikTok, Facebook, or similar platforms. Experience using Canva, CapCut, Adobe Express, Adobe Creative Suite, or other design/editing software. Photography and/or videography experience. Comfortable appearing on camera and engaging with fellow students. Basic understanding of social media analytics. Passion for student involvement and creating engaging digital content. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Creative thinking and storytelling. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Understanding of current social media trends and Gen Z audiences. Attention to detail and ability to receive feedback. Commitment to representing Stephens College professionally across digital platforms. Physical Requirements Ability to move throughout campus to attend and document events. Ability to stand for extended periods during campus programs. Ability to lift up to 25 pounds for event materials when needed. Frequent use of computers, cameras, and mobile devices. Salary Description $15.00/hour Apply Stephens College Work Study Jobs Jobs View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Stephens College Work Study Jobs: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4436530": {
      "title": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs",
      "description": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs - Marketing & Communications Creative Asst - Federal Work Study Students ONLY In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Stephens College Work Study Jobs > Marketing & Communications Creative Asst - Federal Work Study Students ONLY Stephens College Work Study Jobs Apply Marketing & Communications Creative Asst - Federal Work Study Students ONLY Marketing & Communications Apply Job Type Part-time, Temporary Description The Marketing & Communications Student Creative Assistant is a hands-on, career-focused position for a Federal Work Study eligible student interested in marketing, communications, social media, photography, videography, graphic design, and/or creative media. This is real-world creative work, not busywork. Student workers will contribute to projects that support the Stephens College brand and communicate the student experience to prospective students, current students, alumni, families, and the broader community. A major goal of this position is to help students leave with more than work-study hours, they should leave with experience they can use after graduation. The position is designed to help students build professional skills, develop a portfolio, gain experience working with a creative team, and explore careers in marketing and communications. What You’ll Do: Social Media & Content Help create content for Stephens College social media channels. Assist with developing social media ideas, captions, short-form video, Reels, Stories, and other digital content. Attend campus events and capture timely, authentic content. Learn how social content is planned, created, scheduled, published, and evaluated. Identify student stories, campus moments, events, and people that could become compelling content. Photography & Videography Photograph and/or video campus events, students, faculty, programs, and everyday Stephens life. Assist with planned photo and video shoots. Capture both polished marketing content and authentic behind-the-scenes moments. Learn professional practices for lighting, composition, framing, audio, file organization, and visual storytelling. Help select, organize, edit, and prepare images and video for use across marketing channels. Graphic Design Create graphics and visual assets for social media, digital communications, events, and marketing projects. Work within the Stephens College brand standards while developing creative concepts. Assist with layouts, presentations, promotional materials, digital graphics, and other design projects. Gain experience receiving creative direction, responding to feedback, revising work, and preparing final files for production. Marketing & Communications Assist with real campaigns and projects from concept through completion. Help gather information, interview students or campus community members, and identify potential stories. Participate in creative brainstorming and project planning. Learn how different pieces of a marketing campaign work together across print, digital, social, web, email, photography, and video. Collaborate with professional marketing and communications staff and campus partners. Requirements We are looking for a student who is: Creative, curious, and willing to try new things. Interested in marketing, communications, design, photography, video, social media, or related fields. Basic knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite is needed to create portfolio content. Reliable and able to meet deadlines. Willing to take initiative and pitch ideas. Comfortable working independently while also collaborating with a team. Open to feedback and interested in improving their work. Detail-oriented while still thinking creatively. Students will gain tangible experience and work samples they can take into internships, graduate programs, and future careers. Salary Description $15.00/hour Apply Stephens College Work Study Jobs Jobs View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Stephens College Work Study Jobs: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4431779": {
