    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4421673": {
      "title": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs",
      "description": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs - The Children's School Support Staff - Federal Work Study ONLY In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Stephens College Work Study Jobs > The Children's School Support Staff - Federal Work Study ONLY Stephens College Work Study Jobs Apply The Children's School Support Staff - Federal Work Study ONLY The Children's School at Stephens College Apply Job Type Part-time, Temporary Description Federal Work Study eligible students provide part-time support within CSSC. They assist with student supervision and daily routines in morning care, afternoon extended day, nap time coverage, and transitions. These roles are essential in maintaining a safe, nurturing, and well-organized environment for preschool and elementary students. Responsibilities: AM Extended Day (7:30–8:20 AM) Arrive by 7:25 AM to clock in and prepare for student arrival. Set up tables with approved extended day materials (e.g., blocks, Legos, art supplies, games). Ensure that only materials marked for extended day use are accessible. Maintain a calm, supervised indoor environment (playground is closed during AM extended day). Guide students with breakfast routines (eat first, then play). Begin clean-up at 8:10 AM; ensure all students participate and that materials are properly stored. Escort elementary students to Room 107 at 8:15 AM and supervise until 8:20 AM (students must always be supervised). Escort preschool students to their classrooms following the elementary group. Maintain active supervision and avoid cell phone use unless explicitly permitted by a teacher. Elementary (8:20 AM) Accompany students walking to their classrooms. PM Extended Day (3:40–5:30 PM) Provide active supervision during unstructured playtime both indoors and on the playground. Remain attentive and mobile, positioning yourself to always see and support students. Enforce playground safety rules: Slide feet-first only; no climbing up slides; Swing safely front-to-back only; No rocks, sticks, mulch throwing, or unsafe behaviors; Preschool students only on bikes/scooters with helmets. Snack Time (4:30–4:45 PM):  Serve dry snack foods and water; monitor handwashing before snack; Snack is only for enrolled preschool and elementary students; Students may take snack if picked up during this time. If approached by a parent about a child’s day, notify a classroom teacher—do not discuss student performance. Begin final clean-up at 5:00 PM; offer quiet activities (e.g., Legos, coloring) to simplify end-of-day transitions. At 5:30 PM, stack chairs and wipe down tables with disinfecting wipes. Nap Coverage (12:30–2:15 PM) Assist students in preparing for rest with personal items (blanket, pillow, stuffed animal). Support teachers during story time and help settle students. Monitor nap time and offer quiet comfort (e.g., back rubbing) to help children fall asleep. Maintain silence during nap time—no phone use. Homework may be done only after students are asleep. Support students as they begin to wake up around 2:15 PM. General Expectations Always maintain direct supervision of students. Use of cell phones during work time is strictly prohibited unless approved by a supervisor. Demonstrate responsibility, maturity, and professionalism in all interactions with students, families, and staff. Adhere to all school policies, safety procedures, and expectations for conduct. Report structure: Student workers report directly to the Extended Day Supervisor or the Director of CSSC Salary Description $15.00/hour Apply Stephens College Work Study Jobs Jobs View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Stephens College Work Study Jobs: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4415589": {
      "title": "Stephens College",
      "description": "Stephens College - General Maintenance I In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > General Maintenance I Stephens College Apply General Maintenance I Columbia, MO • Campus Facilities Apply Job Type Full-time Description The General Maintenance I position supports the safe, efficient, and attractive operation of Stephens College by performing preventive maintenance, repairs, and general maintenance throughout campus facilities. This position works in academic buildings, residence halls, administrative offices, athletic facilities, and other campus spaces to ensure buildings and equipment are well maintained and ready to support students, faculty, staff, and visitors. The ideal candidate is a dependable, service-oriented professional who enjoys solving problems, working with their hands, and contributing to a positive campus environment. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Perform preventive maintenance and general repairs to campus buildings, equipment, and building systems. Complete maintenance work orders in a timely and professional manner while providing excellent customer service. Perform basic repairs involving carpentry, plumbing, electrical, painting, drywall, flooring, doors, ceilings, windows, locks, changing filters and building hardware. Assist with troubleshooting and repairing HVAC equipment, and building systems as needed. Install, repair, and replace fixtures, shelving, whiteboards, signage, furniture, and other building components. Conduct routine inspections to identify maintenance concerns and recommend corrective actions. Support residence hall maintenance, including room turnovers, repairs, and preparation for student move-in and move-out. Assist with campus events by setting up and taking down tables, chairs, staging, tents, and other event equipment. Assist with office relocations, furniture moves, and departmental requests. Perform seasonal duties such as snow and ice removal, storm cleanup, and exterior maintenance. Maintain tools, equipment, and assigned work areas in a safe and organized manner. Accurately document completed work using the Facilities ticketing system. Follow all College policies and procedures, including OSHA safety standards and proper use of personal protective equipment (PPE). Work collaboratively with other Facilities team members and departments to meet campus needs. Participate in rotating on-call schedule for emergency response and after-hours call-in situations when required. Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements Required High school diploma or equivalent. One to three years of general building maintenance, construction, or related experience. Working knowledge of carpentry, plumbing, electrical, painting, and general building maintenance. Ability to safely operate hand tools, power tools, ladders, lifts, and maintenance equipment. Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills. Excellent communication and customer service skills. Ability to work independently while contributing to a team environment. Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Preferred Experience in commercial, institutional, or higher education facilities maintenance. Experience using computerized maintenance management systems. Knowledge of HVAC systems and preventive maintenance practices. Physical Requirements Frequently lift, carry, push, and pull up to 50 pounds; occasionally lift up to 75 pounds with assistance. Stand, walk, bend, kneel, climb, crawl, and work from ladders or lifts for extended periods. Work indoors and outdoors in varying weather conditions. Safely use maintenance equipment, power tools, and motorized vehicles. Ability to respond to emergency maintenance situations outside normal work hours when necessary. Founded in 1833, Stephens College is the second-oldest women's college in the United States, dedicated to providing innovative, experiential, and career-focused education across various disciplines. Located in Columbia, Missouri, Stephens College continues to be a leader in women's education, fostering a community where students are empowered to lead, innovate, and excel. The college also provides flexible, co-educational master’s degrees and certificates for working professionals, and is home to the co-educational Conservatory for the Performing Arts at Stephens College. Ranked (over and over again) as one of the best college towns in America, Columbia, Missouri, is home to 36,000+ college students and 118,000 residents. Columbia — conveniently located approximately 100 miles from both Kansas City and St. Louis — has it all: big-time college sports, film, music and arts festivals, a high-energy arts community, amazing recreation, and a great downtown with lots of places to eat, shop, snack and check out the latest bands. The Columbia community offers outstanding health care options, as well as excellent educational opportunities for every level of student (including our own Children’s School ). Stephens offers an attractive benefits package that includes health insurance, an Employee Assistance Program, Supplemental Retirement Annuity, Faculty/Staff Grants, tuition waivers and tuition paid undergraduate classes for dependents. Full-time staff work 36 hours and are paid for 40 !! Stephens is an Equal Opportunity Employer and will recruit and employ qualified personnel without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, or status as a veteran. Apply View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Stephens College: Privacy Policy"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4413921": {
      "title": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs",
      "description": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs - Social Media Support - Federal Work Study ONLY In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Stephens College Work Study Jobs > Social Media Support - Federal Work Study ONLY Stephens College Work Study Jobs Apply Social Media Support - Federal Work Study ONLY The Conservatory for the Performing Arts Apply Job Type Part-time, Temporary Description The Conservatory Social Media position for Federal Work Study eligible students will work closely with the Conservatory Director of Recruitment and Retention. This position will gain practical workplace experience in a professional environment. This position provides students with hands-on experience in digital marketing, content creation, branding, and audience engagement while helping strengthen the Conservatory’s online presence. Learning Opportunities: This position provides real-world experience in arts administration, social media strategy and content marketing, design and multimedia production, analytics and performance reporting, professional communication and learning how these functions support organizational goals and daily operations. Responsibilities: Create, schedule, and publish content across social media platforms (e.g., Instagram, Facebook, and TikTok). Develop graphics, photos, videos, and written content that align with the organization's brand and messaging. Assist in planning and executing social media campaigns to promote events, programs, and initiatives. Monitor social media accounts by responding to comments and messages as directed and engaging with followers. Maintain a consistent posting schedule and content calendar. Perform other marketing and communications duties as assigned. Preferred Skills: Available for flexible scheduling Effective communication and time management skills Computer proficiency in all social media modes, Canva, CapCut, etc... Ability to manage multiple tasks and prioritize responsibilities. Dependable, organized, and willing to learn. Professional appearance and demeanor required Availability: Applicants must be available for a minimum of two days per week in two-hour time slots. This position reports to Kristy Simpson, Director of Recruitment & Retention Salary Description $15.00/hour Apply Stephens College Work Study Jobs Jobs View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Stephens College Work Study Jobs: Privacy Policy"
