    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4409221": {
      "title": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs",
      "description": "Stephens College Work Study Jobs - Costume Shop Support - Federal Work Study ONLY In order to use this site, it is necessary to enable JavaScript. Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser . All Jobs > Stephens College Work Study Jobs > Costume Shop Support - Federal Work Study ONLY Stephens College Work Study Jobs Apply Costume Shop Support - Federal Work Study ONLY The Conservatory for the Performing Arts Apply Job Type Part-time, Temporary Description The Conservatory is seeking dependable Federal Work Study eligible student workers to assist in the Conservatory Costume Shop. This role supports the construction, alteration, maintenance, and organization of costumes for departmental productions. The position offers valuable hands-on experience in costume construction and wardrobe support for students seeking employment in costume design/construction, fashion, or positions in wardrobe crews at regional theatres, national tours, and Broadway productions. Learning Opportunities: This position offers practical experience in costume shop operations and the chance to develop valuable skills in sewing, tailoring, garment care, and theatre production support—ideal for students pursuing studies and employment in theatre, costume design, or fashion. Responsibilities: Assist in costume construction, including fitting, cutting, and sewing. Alter existing garments according to designer specifications Help organize and maintain costume stock, accessories, and shop supplies Perform basic costume crafts work (e.g., dyeing, distressing, millinery, painting) Label and track costume pieces for productions Assist with costume changes, quick changes, and wardrobe maintenance during dress rehearsals and performances (as needed) Maintain cleanliness and organization in the costume shop and dressing areas Follow all shop safety procedures and use equipment responsibly Preferred Skills: Basic sewing skills (hand and/or machine) Familiarity with sewing machines, sergers, irons, and related tools Previous experience in costume or fashion-related work Understanding of fabric types and garment construction Strong communication skills Availability: Applicants must be available for a minimum of two afternoons per week in the window of 1pm to 5pm. (ex: 1-3p, 2-4p, 3-5p) This position reports to Montana Carlson, Professor of Costume Design & Production. Salary Description $15.00/hour Apply Stephens College Work Study Jobs Jobs View All Jobs Powered by Privacy Policy | Payroll & HR Software Stephens College Work Study Jobs: Privacy Policy"
    },
